## Screening weighed (test-audience `screening/cut-v1.md`, commit 248015424ea5)

The viewer understood the child, the release, the drift past the village and the light among the stars unprompted, read both cards and heard the ambience and the cue. Their flags, checked against the cut:

1. **05.9–06.2 double lantern (confirmed, fix).** The dissolve from shot 1 to shot 2 superimposes the small lantern of shot 1 on the large lantern of shot 2 (frames from 05.6 s every 4 frames, in the third frame). It is the one moment of confusion. Fix: a straight cut at 06.0 (wide shot to the close-up on the lantern), or a dissolve of no more than 3 frames.
2. **02.0–02.5 title over the child (confirmed, minor fix).** The title is still at about 50 % over the child during the dissolve into shot 1. Fix: finish the title's fade-out before the picture dissolve starts.
3. **16–18 which light is the lantern (no fix).** In full frames (16.8 s) the lantern is the one warm-orange point on the water in the same screen position as in shot 4 (≈0.66 of frame width). "It became one of the lights" is the ending the input asks for.
4. **08–13 slow and static (no fix).** It is a deliberate quiet drift; 3.5 s per shot is inside the spec. Not changing the timing.
5. **19.0–20.0 sound ends before the picture (not confirmed).** Measured: audio −22.3 dB at 19.0, −35.0 at 19.5, −45.1 at 19.75; picture luma 40.5 at 19.0, 23.7 at 19.5, 10.9 at 19.75. They fade together.

**Decision: revise cut-v1 → cut-v2 for items 1 and 2 only (editor), then re-check and lock.** No other position's work changes.
